# stdlib/syntax.llt — Let-softening for fn/class/type (opt-in module)
#
# This module is kept for backward compatibility and documentation purposes.
# The fn, class, and type let-softening macros are now globally registered
# (like tmpl, do, begin) via stdlib/macros.llt and do not require an explicit
# include.
#
# Usage (still works, but not required):
#   [include %libdir "syntax.llt"]
#
# Per unified-bindings.md (Accepted 2026-05-17), [fn [x y] body] (without let)
# SHOULD be a parse error. Currently the parser accepts both forms — this is a
# known bug tracked in TODO.md (unified-bindings-parser-enforcement).
# The macros here handle programmatic macro-output cases where old-form Call
# nodes are produced by other macros.
#
# Eventually (once the parser enforces let-only params):
#   [fn [let x y] body]          only valid source form
#   [fn [x y] body]              parse error — must use [let ...] params
#
# Implementation: see stdlib/macros.llt for the transformer functions
# (syntax-fn, syntax-class, syntax-type) and src/expand.rs for registration.

# Empty dict — including this file adds nothing to scope.
[]
